# Tallyhand environment contract.
# Copy to .env (or run ./install.sh, which writes it for you).
#
# Two knobs select the deployment shape:
#   TALLY_STORAGE = dexie | sqlite | postgres | convex   (default: dexie)
#   TALLY_AUTH    = clerk | builtin | none                (default: none)
#
# Local mode  = sqlite/dexie storage + auth=none → single-user, zero-config.
# Hosted mode = postgres/convex storage OR any real auth → login required,
#               every query scoped by the authenticated user id.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- storage
# dexie    — browser IndexedDB (default; server/API falls back to sqlite).
# sqlite   — local server file backend (zero dependencies). Best local pick.
# postgres — hosted, via Drizzle. Requires DATABASE_URL. Migrations in drizzle/
#            are applied automatically by deploy/entrypoint.sh.
# convex   — hosted, via the Convex TS client. Requires CONVEX_URL.
#            Deploy functions first: `npx convex dev` (see convex/tally.ts).
TALLY_STORAGE=sqlite
TALLY_AUTH=none

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- postgres
# Format: postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST:5432/DATABASE
# The compose stack sets this automatically; set it only for an external DB.
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://tallyhand:secret@db:5432/tallyhand
# Compose-only: password for the bundled Postgres (app uses DATABASE_URL).
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=
# Port the app is published on.
APP_PORT=3000

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ convex
# Deployment URL from `npx convex dev` / dashboard, e.g.
# https://happy-otter-123.convex.cloud
# CONVEX_URL=

# -------------------------------------------------------------------- auth
# clerk   — hosted pick. Create an app at https://dashboard.clerk.com and
#           paste both keys. First admin: Clerk dashboard → user → Public
#           metadata → { "role": "admin" }.
# CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_...
# CLERK_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_...
#
# builtin — self-hoster magic links. Requires TALLY_STORAGE=postgres.
#           Users live in builtin_users; the FIRST user to sign in becomes
#           admin automatically. Needs APP_BASE_URL to build login links.
# BUILTIN_AUTH_SECRET=            # min 32 chars — generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
# APP_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000
#
# Optional SMTP: when unset, one-time login links are printed to the server
# logs on request (standard self-host fallback — forward them yourself).
# SMTP_HOST=
# SMTP_PORT=587
# SMTP_USER=
# SMTP_PASS=
# SMTP_FROM=tallyhand@example.com
# SMTP_SECURE=0                  # set to 1 for SMTPS on port 465

# ------------------------------------------------------------ share links
# Signed public share links (/share/…). Required in hosted mode.
# Rotating this invalidates ALL outstanding share links.
TALLY_SHARE_SECRET=              # min 32 chars — generate with: openssl rand -hex 32

# ------------------------------------------------------- attachments (S3/R2)
# Receipt storage. When S3_*/R2_* is unset, files stay on local disk at
# TALLYHAND_ATTACHMENTS_DIR (compose mounts a persistent volume there).
# Generic S3 (S3_* wins when both are set):
# S3_ENDPOINT=https://s3.amazonaws.com   # or MinIO / Backblaze B2 / etc.
# S3_BUCKET=tallyhand-attachments
# S3_REGION=us-east-1
# S3_ACCESS_KEY=
# S3_SECRET_KEY=
# S3_FORCE_PATH_STYLE=0                  # set to 1 for MinIO
# Cloudflare R2 (cheapest: 10GB + 10M reads/mo free):
# R2_ACCOUNT_ID=
# R2_BUCKET=tallyhand-attachments
# R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# R2_REGION=auto
# TALLYHAND_ATTACHMENTS_DIR=./data/attachments

# ----------------------------------------------- machine / API-token auth
# v1 API machine access in hosted mode: clients send
# `Authorization: Bearer <TALLYHAND_API_TOKEN>`; requests are attributed to
# TALLYHAND_HOSTED_CLI_USER_ID (use the user id from /admin/users).
# TALLYHAND_API_TOKEN=
# TALLYHAND_HOSTED_CLI_USER_ID=
# Personal API tokens: signed-in users (clerk/builtin) can also mint their
# own long-lived tokens in the app at Settings → Connect. Those travel as
# `Authorization: Bearer thp_…`, authenticate /api/v1 and /api/mcp exactly
# like TALLYHAND_API_TOKEN, and are attributed to the token's owner.
# Only the SHA-256 hash is stored (table `api_tokens` in the active
# storage backend).
# Local server sqlite path (TALLY_STORAGE=sqlite only).
# TALLYHAND_DB_PATH=./data/tallyhand.db

# ------------------------------------------------------- Stripe payments
# Online payments on the client portal (/share/[token] Pay button) and via
# POST /api/v1/stripe/payment-links. TEST MODE is the documented default —
# live keys work but are loudly warned about at session creation.
#
# 1. Stripe dashboard → toggle TEST MODE on → Developers → API keys:
#    copy the Secret key (sk_test_…).
# 2. Developers → Webhooks → (in test mode) Add endpoint:
#    https://<your-app>/api/v1/stripe/webhook
#    Events: checkout.session.completed → copy the Signing secret (whsec_…).
# 3. Set the env vars below. On Vercel, app-URL detection falls back to
#    VERCEL_URL automatically; self-hosters set TALLYHAND_APP_URL.
#
# With STRIPE_SECRET_KEY unset, payments stay disabled and the portal shows
# its "payments not configured" state — local mode is unaffected.
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_...
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_...
# TALLYHAND_APP_URL=https://tally.example.com   # self-hosters; Vercel: auto
# NOTE: NEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY is NOT needed — Tallyhand uses
# Stripe-hosted Checkout only (no client-side Stripe.js).
